---
description: Extra rules for sponsor integrations and firmware code.
globs: backend/integrations/**,agents/**,firmware/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# Untrusted input
- Inbound SMS text is untrusted. Parse only an exact match after trim and uppercase: YES or NO. Never pass raw SMS text to Gemini or any LLM, never log it unmasked, never use it in a shell, SQL or file path.
- Webhook handlers must verify what the sponsor docs say to verify (signature or token) if the docs describe one; otherwise restrict to the known sender number and document the limitation in docs/DECISIONS.md.
- Validate all webhook and telemetry payloads with Pydantic; reject unknown shapes with a 4xx and a log entry.
- Telemetry values must be range-checked (power 0-500 W, temperature -20 to 120 C); out-of-range readings are flagged and not used for control decisions.

# LLM usage (Gemini and agents)
- Send only compact summaries, never raw logs or secrets.
- Verify that numbers in generated text exist in the input; otherwise discard and use the templated fallback.
- Agent messages follow the SPEC envelope exactly; a malformed message is dropped and logged, never executed.
- Never let model output change a schedule directly. Only the optimizer or a human approval changes a schedule.

# Human-in-the-loop
- A schedule change affecting more than 0 jobs requires an approved status before it is applied. The only paths to applied are the SMS YES reply and the dashboard Approve button.
- Timeout means expired and the baseline stays.
- Every state transition is written to the decision log with the actor.

# Firmware
- Fail-safe: on lost backend, fan ON.
- Command debounce 5 s; never toggle outputs faster.
- Low-voltage loads only; keep a safety note in the README.
- No blocking delays longer than 100 ms in the main loop.
